WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160
On the 6th of July, the official Elden&nbsp;
Ring website was updated with a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.120
description. It reads as follows:
The Golden Order has been shattered.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.560
Throughout the Lands Between, Demigods holding&nbsp;
shards of the Elden Ring squabble and make war&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.160
over the ruins of a perfect realm, now abandoned&nbsp;
by the golden guidance of the Greater Will.
&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:26.720
As the echoes of this conflict thunder in&nbsp;
the distance, an outcast arrives. Once,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.000
their ancestors called the Lands Between home,&nbsp;
but the blessed light of grace was lost to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.687
their tribe long ago, and they were expelled&nbsp;
from the kingdom. They are the Tarnished,

00:00:36.687 --> 00:00:48.400
and they have returned to claim the Elden&nbsp;
Lordship promised to them by legend.
&nbsp; 
Those few inhabitants who are not mad or hostile linger near the broken remnants&nbsp;
of cities left behind by the Shattering. They may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:54.320
have answers for you, if you help them. Above them&nbsp;
all, ensconced in legacies bristling with traps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.560
secrets, and guardians, the Demigods - warped&nbsp;
Lords who began as members of a royal and noble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.480
family - rule their domains with the unyielding&nbsp;
power granted by shards of the Elden Ring.
 
&nbsp;

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.160
This is probably all the story we're going to get&nbsp;
until Gamescom at the end of August, and combined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:18.240
with everything else, it's actually a ton to go&nbsp;
over, so I've shattered it all into 8 sections.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.640
Let's get into it, starting with&nbsp;
the character they're building up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.040
as the big boss of Elden Ring. 
Her name is Queen Marika, the Eternal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.720
She's first mentioned on the official site, which&nbsp;
reads "In the Lands Between ruled by Queen Marika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.800
the Eternal, the Elden Ring, the source of the&nbsp;
Erdtree, has been shattered. Marika's offspring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:47.040
demigods all, claimed the shards of the Elden Ring&nbsp;
known as the Great Runes, and the mad taint of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.480
their newfound strength triggered a war. 
The Japanese word they use for "Eternal"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:58.400
is the same one used to describe the&nbsp;
"perpetuity" of the Everlasting Dragons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:06.000
so she likely has a sort of immortality, like&nbsp;
them. Her offspring are demigods, after all, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.520
it would make sense that she's a sort of deity.
Now, it is still possible that Marika is innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:19.360
in all of this, and that her offspring alone&nbsp;
are responsible for the shattering. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:25.120
a Russian site calls her the "mistress of the&nbsp;
coveted ring", which I think suggests she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:31.520
claimed at least some of it's power...and assuming&nbsp;
she's still the ruler of the Lands Between,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:35.040
it is at least being implied&nbsp;
that she has benefited from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.440
and played a part in, the ring's shattering. 
From what we can tell, the reasons for shattering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:46.160
the Elden Ring so far are 
a) to claim its power, but also
&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:55.360
b) to upset the world order and inspire chaos.
Because despite Marika "ruling" the Lands Between,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:12.960
her demigod offspring are actually squabbling&nbsp;
with one another, and "making war". According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.800
to an interview with Miyazaki, each demigod&nbsp;
can be found at the end of Legacy dungeons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.960
and since there is one legacy dungeon per open&nbsp;
world, that means each demigod likely has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:31.460
chunk of the open world under their dominion.&nbsp;
This sort of drama between kingdoms is part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:38.080
and parcel of George R. R. Martin's writing, and&nbsp;
since we're expected to "delve into the complex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:43.120
bloody history of the Shattering", I expect&nbsp;
there to be a ton of lore behind each demigod.
&nbsp;

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.320
A large part of the designs of these these&nbsp;
major characters will be how they were twisted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.760
by claiming shards of the Elden Ring. According&nbsp;
to Miyazaki, "they each inherited a different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:59.280
power or element, so to speak, and each&nbsp;
was twisted and warped in its own way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.400
and it brought a tainted strength to each of&nbsp;
them. They each fell to madness and fell to ruin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.840
in their own individual ways. So while there&nbsp;
is heroic and mythological elements to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.560
they are also going to have this very mad&nbsp;
taint and this deep-seated ruin to them."
&nbsp;

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:20.000
And it seems like one such lord has already&nbsp;
been revealed to us. This heavily armed boss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.160
is referenced in a tweet from June 24th, which&nbsp;
reads "A lord clings to his ruined legacy; the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:32.320
ruler of a husk wrung dry by war". While I guess&nbsp;
it's possible he's a lord from the world before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:38.560
the shattering clinging to his ruined legacy,&nbsp;
it's still more likely that he's a demigod,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:43.760
since he's a perfect example of a character that&nbsp;
might be tainted and ruined by the Elden Ring. 
&nbsp;

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:50.480
And you have to wonder..did any of them, including&nbsp;
Marika, expect the Elden Ring to twist and taint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.200
them in such a way? Do they even care?
According to the official site, the shards of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.200 --> 00:05:02.160
the Elden Ring are called "Great runes". Runes&nbsp;
are simply a type of alphabet, but in fantasy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:08.800
writing they're often used as words of magical&nbsp;
power. Together, it seems, these runes "spell",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:15.120
the Elden Ring..but since the Elden Ring has been&nbsp;
shattered, alone, some of these runes have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:20.640
claimed. A long, long time ago, the earliest&nbsp;
leak about Elden Ring actually revealed the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:27.760
was once called "Great Rune", said to be a game&nbsp;
about travelling to distant kingdoms and claiming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:34.480
the power that lies there. Therefore, I wonder if&nbsp;
defeating a demigod might allow you to claim their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:41.920
power in some way, perhaps getting a specific&nbsp;
ability or powerup? Accroding to the trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:47.680
the Elden Ring IS a weapon, after all..
Brandish the Elden Ring..
&nbsp;

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.000
For all of us. 
They've done an excellent job with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:01.120
concept of the Elden Ring, because even though we&nbsp;
know so much about it, it's still hard to pin down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:08.000
exactly what it is. It's made up of runes, making&nbsp;
it literal..it gives order to the world, making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:15.120
it seem conceptual..and yet it's also so physical,&nbsp;
able to be hammered and shattered into pieces. 
&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:23.600
One wonderful discovery is how similar&nbsp;
the shattering scene with the blacksmith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:30.880
is to this "forging of the ring" concept art by&nbsp;
Alan Lee, who has done a lot of official artwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:40.480
for Tolkien's "Lord of the Rings" series. Like&nbsp;
the "One Ring", the Elden Ring also has text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:47.680
upon it..it's also a weapon of great power,&nbsp;
and perhaps most importantly - it also has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:51.360
a will associated with it.
According to the official site,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.640
when the demigods triggered the "Shattering"&nbsp;
war, they were abandoned by the "Greater Will".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:04.400
Somehow, this "Greater Will" persists despite the&nbsp;
ring being shattered, and has decided that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:10.240
demigods, once members of a royal and noble&nbsp;
family, are no longer worthy of its favor.
&nbsp;

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:16.880
Instead, it seems, this favor has been&nbsp;
returned to us instead: the Tarnished.
&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:17.304
"And now the guidance of grace will be brought&nbsp;
to the Tarnished who were spurned by the grace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.304 --> 00:07:19.920
of gold and exiled from the Lands Between."
According to Miyazaki, "you could call them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.880
tarnished individuals who have lost grace. And&nbsp;
this was a long time preceding the setting of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:30.160
the game, a long time before. The ancestors of&nbsp;
the characters that are present in the world were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.840
banished and exiled from The Lands Between, these&nbsp;
Tarnished. Then a long time after that, the Elden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.480
Ring was shattered in a historical event. This&nbsp;
triggers the return of this lost grace and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

